# Wave W17-V (Route 206): pillar turf — pillar-shadow meadow: a cool green carrying blue-green shade flecks, the meadow that lives under the cycleway’s stone shadow and never quite warms (design: the elevated cycleway crosses on pillars; the miners’ cave sleeps in its shadow). Route 206’s own ground — split from Route 205’s wind-combed valley green by temperature (pillar shade vs open wind) and from Route 110’s pond meadow (Maris) by register: this meadow is shadowed by stone, that one open to its shore.
